Bugfix: Legacy OCS routes answered with empty data once the route cache was warm

With the route cache active (default), every /ocs/v1.php route of the old
API style - the provisioning API (cloud/users, cloud/groups, cloud/apps) and
the sharing API (apps/files_sharing/api/v1/shares) - answered with status 100
and an empty "data" after the first request had filled the cache, and the
log filled with "Undefined array key" from lib/private/legacy/api.php. The
cache kept the static action ['OC_API', 'call'] of those routes, so the
router took them for ready-to-use routes and skipped loading the owner app
whose routes.php registers the actual handlers. Such routes are now
recognised by their list of owner apps in the cache and go through the same
reload path as routes without an action; 'core' and 'settings' are skipped
as owners because they are no loadable apps.
